04160688665710186,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":38.4,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.16443857030375375,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":67.3,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.041807150923770936,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":47.7,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.05304846376986501,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":26.5,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.5482327417882985,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":8.6,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.20690842972965934,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.5667699128611996,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06676377015908426,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":85.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.008043460784796563,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":39.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.030090972708187544,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":49.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.025559999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":17.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Wyndham Hotels & Resorts, Inc. is the world's largest hotel franchising company by the number of franchised properties, with approximately 8,300 hotels across approximately 100 countries on six continents. Through its network of over 855,000 rooms appealing to the everyday traveler, Wyndham commands a leading presence in the economy and midscale segments of the lodging industry. The Company operates a portfolio of 25 hotel brands, including Super 8, Days Inn, Ramada, Microtel, La Quinta, Baymont, Wingate, AmericInn, ECHO Suites, Registry Collection Hotels, Trademark Collection and Wyndham. Wyndham Hotels & Resorts, Inc. was incorporated in 2017 and is headquartered in Parsippany, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Geoffrey A. Ballotti | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $714K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $160K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $22K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Wyndham Hotels & Resorts, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $5.9B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 8% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $321M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.90\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.6% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 42% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.41868738882127166},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (36% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 21% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Wyndham Hotels & Resorts (NYSE:WH) Insider Scott Strickland Sells 12,000 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/wyndham-hotels-resorts-nysewh-insider-scott-stricklan